<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="70a33fa2">&lt;h4&gt;
    Business Engagement Measures
&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Indicators and metrics that identify and monitor the level of business ownership and involvement for preparing,
    managing, and implementing change.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;
    Business Readiness Metrics
&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    A list that includes readiness categorized by stabilization goals, client pain points and change impacts.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;
    Business Adoption Metrics
&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Includes measures and indicators of sustained and disciplined use of the business solution, system, and procedures.
    This section&apos;s content aids understanding if the business solution is implemented and operationalized,
    whether the change is demonstrating expected business outcomes and realizing business benefits.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="5166e7b7"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="e7e773d4"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="c613af0"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="ca03e9c0">To provide a means for measuring the levels of business engagement, readiness, and adoption; to proactively identify
people-related issues and implementation risks; to validate if people are engaged and prepared for business solution
implementation; to validate that the business solution is operationalized by the right people in the right role; to
understand the correlation between observable use and attainment of expected business outcomes.</attribute>
<attribute name="impactOfNotHaving" nodeId="47fa503a"></attribute>
<attribute name="reasonsForNotNeeding" nodeId="292e3af9"></attribute>
<attribute name="briefOutline" nodeId="7bb65a3c">&lt;p&gt;
    This work product includes criteria, measures, and metrics for:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Business engagement
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Business readiness
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Business adoption
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
